{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Whatever touches.</b> [It is] the flesh of the hattat that shall be holy to His name, and the priest shall eat it; therefore the portion of the one who sprinkles is like the portion of all his brothers." "<b>יזה.</b> R. Moses the Priest said that it is like יטה in the qal binyan, and in its pausal form the yod [is] from the heavy [letters], and the hidden letter is nun. And likewise ויז מדמ׳‎ אל הקיר, in ḥiriq with ויז in pausal form — only in the word נטה, which refers to the wall, in ḥiriq with ויז, it is in ṣere in the qal binyan. And likewise we find ויז נצחם in the qal binyan. And he analyzed well." "And because the hattat is holy, HaShem commanded to wash the place where its blood fell on the garment. <b>In a holy place</b> — this is the courtyard of the Tent of Meeting, for there is a distinction between holy and pure:" "<b>Wherever it splashes upon it.</b> It lacks [the word] מקום ['place'] or ['either']. And the meaning: or if it splashes again upon it — which is the flesh — the priest shall wash the flesh and afterward eat it. Or its meaning is: the place where the blood splashes — you shall wash [it], and בגד ['garment'] will be both feminine and masculine; and like it: אשר תשיג ידו. And the tav of תכבס [is] 'for the priest.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "The Hebrew is elliptical and compressed throughout this comment; translated hyper-literally without smoothing. The comparisons between יזה/יטה forms and their respective vowel patterns are rendered as Ibn Ezra presents them.", 3 "The final clause 'ותי״ו תכבס לכהן' is compressed and its syntax is ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally. The reference is to the feminine tav of תכבס being understood as distributed 'to the priest,' though the precise argument remains cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:55.062735182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}